  "scope": "Two representative 100-season workloads, with real youth/recovery round training in the active profile, a settled round-23 checkpoint after the century in both profiles, an own design applied through the club-identity command at each active season start (101 edits) and a pending match-kit choice in the active round-23 checkpoint that both resumed careers wear and use up, recorded appearances compared before and after every such command, eight-country archive/capacity checks and a separate 1950–2025 era probe. Both careers track their own managers from the founding; the active one also hires a free manager every tenth season and four times a century appoints, replaces and reappoints on one day, beside the interims contract ends leave. At the century and the round after it, every tenure, outcome source, date and record link round-trips the checkpoint exactly, and the records room's paged manager-history read covers every tenure and attributed match. Every checkpoint must round-trip the complete canonical world without loss; save limits and history retention remain unchanged. Throughput includes codec/replay checks; peak heap is sampled at checkpoints. No claim that all seeds/actions fit indefinitely. Direct engine harness records but does not stop at UI warnings."
